{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a ruler who lived during the 12th century. He was the Prince of Antioch and ruled over Tripoli from 1168 until his death in 1187. He was the son of the Prince of Antioch Bohemond III and was appointed regent by his father in 1166. \n\n* **Early Life ** \n  Raymond III was born around 1145. He was the son of Bohemond III and his wife Constance of Hauteville. He was the brother of Bohemond IV and Sibylla of Jerusalem. His family was of Normandy and Sicilian origin. \n\n* **Reign ** \n  Raymond III became Prince of Antioch in 1166 after the death of his father. In 1168 he was appointed regent of Tripoli. He became the Count of Tripoli in 1172 after the death of the last ruler of the Banu Hum tribe. His reign was marked by conflicts with the Ayyubid dynasty. \n\n* **Military Campaigns ** \n  In 1171 Raymond III led a successful military campaign against the Ayyubid dynasty and reconquered parts of Tripoli. He also led a campaign against the Ayyubid dynasty in 1172 and was successful in the Battle of Montgisard. He later led an unsuccessful campaign against the Ayyubid dynasty in 1177.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1985016018152237}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.194758028257638e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002616301644593477}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.01988795096986e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.007840453647077084}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.36228299140930176}, {"token": " ruler", "logprob": -1.9227761030197144}, {"token": " who", "logprob": -5.3695526123046875}, {"token": " lived", "logprob": -0.5059874057769775}, {"token": " during", "logprob": -2.7070062160491943}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.000153768167365342